From a330dce52005a341e0041ab036875fb77c17cbbe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 13:50:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] Amiga: no UNIX permission headers beside the protection
 byte

An Amiga build wrote the file's protection bits twice: in the header's
attribute byte, as Amiga LhA does, and as a UNIX mode in extended header
0x50 (with 0x51 uid/gid and 0x52/0x53 names), made by the C library from
the same bits without h, s, p and a. The two disagreed (a file without
the e bit got mode 0711), and readers that prefer 0x50 restored the wrong
bits: XAD on AROS gave hs---we- for sp-rw-d.

On Amiga builds only the time stamp extension 0x54 is written now, on
level 1 as before; level 2 keeps its time in the base header.

Repository: lha (https://github.com/sodero/lha.git)
Base: 1e7c8f1fc1bd0f72610ca381e21bbda9325cd4f5
Requires: none
Scope: Amiga builds (_AMIGA)
Tested: AROS One 1.3, ABIv11 x86_64 (2026-10-18): a 1229-entry Amiga tree packed and read back identically by Unarc (XAD), and by C:lha except comments, which it does not set; Amiga LhA 2.15, LHa for UNIX and 7-Zip test it OK
Upstream-Status: candidate (not submitted)
Removal: when sodero/lha carries an equivalent change and the pin moves past it
---
 src/header.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/header.c b/src/header.c
index 3b36cdf..426d112 100755
--- a/src/header.c
+++ b/src/header.c
@@ -1659,6 +1659,19 @@ static void
 write_unix_info(hdr)
     LzHeader *hdr;
 {
+#if _AMIGA
+    /* An Amiga archive carries the protection bits in the attribute byte, as
+       Amiga LhA writes it. A UNIX mode beside it (made from the same bits by
+       the C library, without h, s, p and a) said something else, and readers
+       that prefer extension 0x50, XAD among them, restored the wrong bits.
+       Only the time stamp is kept: it is exact to the second. */
+    if (hdr->header_level == 1) {
+        put_word(7);        /* size */
+        put_byte(0x54);     /* time stamp */
+        put_longword(hdr->unix_last_modified_stamp);
+    }
+    return;
+#endif
     /* UNIX specific informations */
 
     put_word(5);            /* size */
